# Ask before commit and push

After finishing a task that changed the repo (bug fix, feature, refactor, docs, icons, CI), **stop and ask**. Do not commit or push until the user says yes.

If they say no, leave the working tree as-is so they can keep stacking fixes and features.

Skip the ask when nothing is dirty, or the turn was only Q&A.

## What to ask

Propose one Conventional Commit subject (and a one-line body only if the why is not obvious). State the **semver bump this message will cause** after push. Current version is the latest fetched `v*` tag (`git fetch --tags`, then `git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match 'v[0-9]*'`, or `scripts/semver.sh` after a pull). Do **not** read `MARKETING_VERSION` in `project.pbxproj` — that file stays `1.0.0` / `10000` locally. An unfetched clone will lie.

- `fix:` / `docs:` / `chore:` / unprefixed → **patch** (`1.3.0` → `1.3.1`)
- `feat:` → **minor** (`1.3.0` → `1.4.0`)
- `feat!:` / `fix!:` or `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer → **major** (`1.3.0` → `2.0.0`)

If the session mixed a feature and a fix, use `feat:` (highest bump). Example ask:

> Commit and push to `main` as `fix: keep settings window in front` (patch → `1.3.1`)? Say **yes** to ship, or keep going.

## If they say yes

1. Follow the repo git commit protocol (status, diff, log, HEREDOC message, no `--no-verify`, no amend unless they asked). Never add `Co-authored-by:`, `Made-with: Cursor`, or any AI credit unless the user explicitly asks.
2. Do **not** hand-edit `MARKETING_VERSION` / tags / `CHANGELOG.md`. Versioning and the changelog section are `scripts/semver.sh` + `.github/workflows/release.yml` on push to `main`.
3. Push `HEAD` to `origin` with `-u` if needed. That publish job tags `vX.Y.Z` and uploads `Zoomie.zip`.
4. Confirm the remote and the expected tag.
5. After the release job finishes, `git pull --ff-only origin main` and `git fetch --tags` so local `CHANGELOG.md` and the new tag match CI.

## If they say no

Do not commit, push, tag, or bump versions. Continue the next request on the same uncommitted work.
